  "_note": [
    "MEASURED LIVE. 154:132 is the same root list as 154:26 in Beginner mode, and",
    "Beginner is the panel's default (`useDSModeOptional()?.mode !== \"pro\"`), so",
    "the state needs no interaction beyond opening the panel. The one thing that",
    "distinguishes the board is the footnote at 154:185/154:186.",
    "",
    "WHAT THE BOARD WON:",
    "  the footnote's words. It shipped as \"Basic mode hides what you cannot edit",
    "  yet. Switch to Pro to unlock.\" \u2014 a sentence that named the mode by a word",
    "  the toggle beside it does not use (the control says Beginner) and described",
    "  what is hidden as \"what you cannot edit yet\". 154:186 says \"Beginner hides",
    "  token IDs and empty foundations. Switch to Pro to show them.\", which names",
    "  both of the things the mode actually hides (`filterTokensByMode` drops",
    "  non-semantic tokens; TokensSection folds empty foundation kinds behind one",
    "  disclosure row).",
    "  Everything in surfaces/brand-lint-warnings.json's `WHAT THE BOARD WON`",
    "  applies here too \u2014 it is one chassis under four state boards.",
    "",
    "NOT CONFORMED \u2014 A CONTRAST FLOOR THE BOARD CANNOT WAIVE:",
    "  154:186 colours the footnote `--color/ink-muted` (#6B7280) on 154:185's",
    "  `--color/bg-subtle` (#F3F4F6) fill. Measured by measure.mjs, that pair is",
    "  4.39:1 at 11px against a 4.5 WCAG AA floor \u2014 a FAIL, and it is what shipped",
    "  before this pass too, unmeasured. The code now paints `--bk-ink-soft`",
    "  (#4B5563), the same substitution `DesignTabFooter` already documents for the",
    "  same pair on the same fill. The board keeps the fill, the 11/16 type and the",
    "  248 measure; it does not get the colour.",
    "  So 154:186 is SKIPPED rather than joined: its four properties are one node,",
    "  and three of them agree. Joining it would fail on `color`; conforming to it",
    "  would put a measured AA failure behind a green gate.",
    "",
    "NOT JOINED, same as the sibling recipes:",
    "  154:132 itself (the drawer's edge, not the panel's) and 1691:7219 (the",
    "  preview band's 82px Figma text-metric height). See",
    "  surfaces/brand-lint-warnings.json for the full reasoning."
  ]
